// Title: Creation Exe for Service with Unquoted Path
// Sigma ID: 8c3c76ca-8f8b-4b1d-aaf3-81aebcd367c9
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-12-30 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547.009
// Description: Adversaries may execute their own malicious payloads by hijacking vulnerable file path
//   references. Adversaries can take advantage of paths that lack surrounding quotations by placing
//   an executable in a higher level directory within the path, so that Windows will choose the
//   adversary's executable to launch.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1574.009/T1574.009.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_creation_unquoted_service_path.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath =~ "C:\\program.exe"
